From 3a896035ff907402a0f58f45ec645cc18343d49b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xbox360 Blades <xbox360-blades@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 10:32:40 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 23/53] Guide: xam's keyframe easing; AddXboxLive's Back and
 box hand-offs

- Easing: xam turns a key's EaseIn/EaseOut/EaseScale into a cubic Bezier
  (8191E1A0: control points (scale, 0) turned by (1 - in) pi/4 and
  (1, 1) - (scale, 0) turned by (1 - out) pi/4) and uses its y at the
  linear progress (8190EA40). This replaces the quadratic stand-ins for
  every Guide slide (EaseIn 100 / EaseOut 100 / both at scale 50).
- AddXboxLive: each step's work is done when its status ends (its task
  completing). B (90103980 -> 90102CE8) does nothing while the profile is
  created, after that cancels and goes back to Save Gamer Profile
  (hudbkgnd HalfToFull, 75-119, with that page's legends moving in); a
  cancelled sign-in is done again on the next pass.
- Box hand-offs from createprofile's box callback (90102040, run from the
  HUD's box close 818D5A18): Test Connection -> Exit Session replaces the
  box in place (the HUD stays in Error); Cancel/No -> ErrorToFull.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
